{title: Onward, Christian Soldiers}
{artist: Sabine Baring-Gould / Arthur S. Sullivan}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening, Closing}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 108}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]Onward, Christian [Bb7]soldiers, [Eb]marching as to [Ab]war
With the [Eb]cross of [Bb7]Jesus [Eb]going on be[Bb7]fore
[Eb]Christ, the royal [Bb7]Master, [Eb]leads against the [Ab]foe
[Eb]Forward into [Bb7]battle, [Eb]see His ban[Bb7]ners [Eb]go
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Eb]Onward, Christian [Bb7]soldiers, [Eb]marching as to [Ab]war
With the [Eb]cross of [Bb7]Jesus [Eb]going on be[Bb7]fore[Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]At the sign of [Bb7]triumph [Eb]Satan's host doth [Ab]flee
[Eb]On then, Christian [Bb7]soldiers, [Eb]on to vic[Bb7]to[Eb]ry
[Eb]Hell's foundations [Bb7]quiver [Eb]at the shout of [Ab]praise
[Eb]Brothers, lift your [Bb7]voices, [Eb]loud your an[Bb7]thems [Eb]raise
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]Like a mighty [Bb7]army [Eb]moves the church of [Ab]God
[Eb]Brothers, we are [Bb7]treading [Eb]where the saints have [Bb7]trod
[Eb]We are not di[Bb7]vided, [Eb]all one body [Ab]we
[Eb]One in hope and [Bb7]doctrine, [Eb]one in char[Bb7]i[Eb]ty
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Eb]Crowns and thrones may [Bb7]perish, [Eb]kingdoms rise and [Ab]wane
[Eb]But the church of [Bb7]Jesus [Eb]constant will re[Bb7]main
[Eb]Gates of hell can [Bb7]never [Eb]'gainst that church pre[Ab]vail
[Eb]We have Christ's own [Bb7]promise, [Eb]and that cannot [Bb7]fail[Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Eb]Onward then, ye [Bb7]people, [Eb]join our happy [Ab]throng
[Eb]Blend with ours your [Bb7]voices [Eb]in the triumph [Bb7]song
[Eb]Glory, laud, and [Bb7]honor [Eb]unto Christ the [Ab]King
[Eb]This through countless [Bb7]ages [Eb]men and angels [Bb7]sing[Eb]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
